# Review-loop scratch — captured diffs, regenerable, but tracked on purpose.
# `.roster/review/` is NOT ignored: reviewers are readonly (read, grep, glob,
# no exec), so a reviewer handed a diff path it cannot open has no way to
# reconstruct it, and Devin background subagents and Gemini-based harnesses
# skip git-ignored paths during file discovery entirely — an ignored review
# directory returns ### Blocked reports and costs a cycle. The capture command
# in AGENTS.md step 4 excludes this directory from `git diff` so a tracked
# review dir does not embed the previous cycle's diff into the next capture.
# The ledger and its archive are tracked for the same recovery reason as before.
#
# (Left intentionally empty — no ignore rule for .roster/review/.)
.superpowers/

# prisma generated client
/src/generated/

# captured mail from E2E runs
/.next/mail.log
